s in evidence_refs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"For fixed square-integrable controls under independent common-population iid samples, the stated variance decomposition, conditional-mean oracle variance, excess rho*Var(g-m)/n and unrestricted affine projection gap hold. They are not measured oracle attainment or validity of the fitted-control interval.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"result.top_program_01\"\n    ],\n    \"citation_keys\": [],\n    \"evidence_refs\": [\n      \"source_evidence/calibration/METHOD.md\",\n      \"source_evidence/calibration/study.py#L12-L26\"\n    ],\n    \"source_role\": \"Registry source is an archived-method path anchor only; its scalar score does not substantiate implementation details or final source identity. Inspect the readable files in evidence_refs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The separate unmeasured bounded construction uses empirical-Bernstein radii with log(4/delta), support lengths, singleton/full-range fallback, delta=alpha/(2K), and fixed nonnegative aggregation. A conditional union-bound coverage argument assumes independent iid common-population samples. These endpoints are not the primary returned track.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"result.top_program_01\"\n    ],\n    \"citation_keys\": [\n      \"MaurerPontil2009\",\n      \"Hoeffding1963\"\n    ],\n    \"evidence_refs\": [\n      \"source_evidence/calibration/program.py#L109-L185\",\n      \"source_evidence/calibration/METHOD.md\"\n    ],\n    \"source_role\": \"Registry source is an archived-method path anchor only; its scalar score does not substantiate implementation details or final source identity. Inspect the readable files in evidence_refs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"An affine-only matched function and oracle reporting helper are present but have no supplied measured results. No new experiments, bootstrap, jackknife or sensitivity sweep were run during drafting.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"result.top_program_01\",\n      \"final.evid